      "content": "A signalized intersection typically offers higher throughput during peak hours due to precise timing, whereas a large roundabout prioritizes systemic friction reduction by forcing slower speeds and yielding rights to approaching traffic. While signals can handle high volumes efficiently with advanced predictive technologies, roundabouts provide more consistent flow and reduced congestion hazards by eliminating queuing at specific points. Ultimately, the choice depends on whether your priority is maximizing capacity through timed controls or enhancing resilience and safety through continuous, variable flow management.",
